 shukla2020-honey-prayagraj-metals,wiki/sources,AUTO_auto-mineral-water-tas-product_2020_10-35535-acpa-2020-0004,pending,2026-05-30T19:44:27.588Z,audited-revised,REVISE,2026-06-09,"Autonomous audit cycle: Checks 2/4/5 clean; Check 3 had one ❌ finding (applied); Check 1 had one ❌ finding (rejected as false positive). Applied: rewrote Methods (brief) section to record the actual instrumentation (Perkin Elmer Analyst 700 AAS) and certified testing lab (University of Allahabad Prayagraj) which the prior page falsely claimed the paper did not disclose; also noted the missing digestion/CRM/recovery data so analytical traceability is honest. Rejected: subagent claim that Table 3 showed Cu detections (H6 0.27 H11 0.02 H13 0.02 H14 0.04) and an As detection (H6 0.01) — independently verified via pdftotext extraction of Table 3 page 131 that Cu (mg/kg) and As (mg/kg) rows are BLD across all 14 samples matching the abstract and conclusion. The subagent was misled by an uncertain table summary I included in the audit prompt. Independent verification catches: Materials and Methods section panel listing '(Cd Pb Cu As)' confirms the recurring 'Pd' label is a typo for Pb (not just an abstract artefact); Verification notes strengthened with this cross-reference. Cd/Pb numerical fidelity confirmed against abstract conclusion and Table 3."
 wu2021-edible-salt-soy-sauce-pb-cd,wiki/sources,AUTO_auto-salt-cd-product_2021_10-46770-as-2020-196,pending,2026-05-30T19:44:27.588Z,audited-revised,REVISE,2026-06-09,"Autonomous audit cycle: Checks 3/4/5 clean; Check 1 had one ⚠️ truncated-table-row concern, Check 2 had two ⚠️ slug-precedent concerns. Applied: (1) filled in soy-sauce Cd spiked row in Key numbers table (added 0.05 mg/kg, found 0.059 mg/kg, recovery 94.0%, RSD 0.23%) from PDF p.4 Table 2, corroborated by paper prose; (2) normalized matrix slug from 'edible-salt' to 'salt' to match established precedent (shindoh2010, sanou-bara2024, et al.); (3) added [[ingredients/salt]] to the Wiki-pages-touched body list for consistency with ingredients frontmatter; (4) updated Verification notes to reflect that the truncated row was recovered during audit. Rejected: none. No independent-verification catches beyond audit findings. Numerical fidelity otherwise verified across abstract LODs, linearity, precision/recovery ranges, and Table 2 spike-recovery values for salt Pb/Cd and soy-sauce Pb."
 hossain2024-rice-cadmium-soil-ph,wiki/sources,AUTO_auto-salt-cd-product_2024_10-53808-kus-2024-21-01-1133-ls,pending,2026-06-09T00:00:00Z,audited-revised,REVISE,2026-06-09,"Autonomous audit cycle: Checks 4/5 clean; Check 1 ⚠️ (Heera 1% OM soil-bioavailable was unfilled placeholder; pH headline values omitted); Check 2 ❌ (mitigation/cadmium-soil-management invented slug); Check 3 ⚠️ (Methods underspecified). Applied: replaced mitigation/cadmium-soil-management with mitigation/agronomic (existing page covers soil pH + OM levers); expanded Key numbers with full Table 2 (pH series, 4 cultivars × 3 pH) and full Table 3 (OM series including Heera 0.59 mg/kg soil-bioavailable Cd); added TF and HQ summary (HQ>1 except BRRI 28 at 3% OM); expanded Methods with Shimadzu AAS AA-7000, HNO3:HClO4 (2:1) at 180°C, STATISTIX v10.0, QA/QC details (permitted per 2026-05-17 scientific-method exception); added Verification note clarifying sample_n=36 basis (4 varieties × 3 pH × 3 OM unique cells) and cultivar-not-brand status. Routing audit clean (not in unresolved/malformed). No rejected findings; no independent-verification catches beyond audit findings."
