+samsiyah2019-indonesia-salt-lead,wiki/sources,AUTO_auto-salt-pb-product_2019_10-20473-jipk-v11i1-11058,pending,2026-05-30T19:44:27.588Z,audited-revised,REVISE,2026-06-09,"Autonomous audit cycle: Checks 2/4/5 clean; Check 1 had one ⚠️ (sample_n null); Check 3 had one ❌ (Methods asserted analytical details were not visible when the Material dan Metode section on journal p45 was fully extractable from the PDF). Applied: (1) set sample_n=28 and expanded sample_population to name the 5 Pamekasan subdistricts; (2) rewrote Methods to include AAS at BBLK Surabaya, SNI 19-0428 (1998) sampling protocol with spear into coded zip bags, n=28 villages across Tlanakan/Galis/Pademawu/Pasean/Batumarmar subdistricts, regulatory comparators SNI 3556-2010 and SNI 7387-2009 (both 10 ppm Pb max), and observation+interview production-stage data collection; (3) updated Verification notes to confirm methods and n verified, and to flag the source-internal Figure 1 Y-axis label inconsistency (mg/l vs ppm in text). Numerical fidelity verified: 0.066 ppm (Lembung), 0.162 ppm (Pangereman), 10 ppm SNI cap, and 12.2 mg/kg landfill background reference (correctly attributed as Kristiyaningsih & Sudarmaji 2008, not Pamekasan). No findings rejected. No independent-verification catches beyond the subagent's findings."
