Hazard Index of Heavy Metals in Artificially Ripened Fruits
Figure 1 shows the hazard index (HI) of the metals of the artificially ripened fruits. The HI calculated for bananas,
pineapple and oranges for adults and children respectively are 0.1115, 0.0200; 0.0111, 0.0191 and 0.0123,
0.0213. HI levels were higher in children than in adults.

